    Bug 2034737 - Fix saving subscriptions when the subscribe dialog is filtered. r=darktrojan,mkmelin


    Bug 2020869 migrated the subscribe dialog to use the new tree-view
    component. When a search filter is applied, the SubscribeDataAdapter
    flattens the hierarchy by creating cloned instances of the matching
    TreeDataRow objects.

    Because the UI modifies the `checked` property on these clones, the
    changes are lost when `subscribeOK()` iterates over the original,
    unmodified hierarchical rows (`_allRowMap`) to collect the final
    subscription changes for the server.

    This patch fixes the desynchronization by:
    1. Retaining a reference to the source row (`originalRow`) when
       cloning rows for the search filter.
    2. Performing a synchronization pass in `subscribeOK()` to map the
       `checked` properties from the active search clones back to their
       original rows in the master list before calculating changes.

    A new test case has been added to `browser_subscribe.js` to ensure
    toggling subscriptions while a search filter is active works as expected.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D296303

